+### 4.3 list_sessions
+
+Requests a list of the user's conversations. The list is always for the authenticated user of the connection; any `userId` field in the frame is ignored ([validated by: answers list_sessions for the authenticated user with ISO dates, forwarding limit and before while ignoring any client userId](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L39)).
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "list_sessions",
+  "limit": 10,
+  "before": {
+    "updatedAt": "2026-01-15T14:30:00Z",
+    "sessionId": "s1"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+| Field    | Type   | Required | Description                   |
+| -------- | ------ | -------- | ----------------------------- |
+| `type`   | string | Yes      | `"list_sessions"`             |
+| `limit`  | number | No       | Max entries to return (1-200) |
+| `before` | object | No       | Cursor for pagination         |
+
+Constraints:
+
+- `limit`, when present, MUST be an integer between 1 and 200.
+- `before`, when present, MUST be an object with a `sessionId` (1-128 characters) and an `updatedAt` (string or number) that parses as a valid date.
+- Violation of these constraints results in an `error` response with code `INVALID_MESSAGE` ([validated by: accepts a bare list_sessions frame and rejects a malformed limit or before with INVALID_MESSAGE without calling listFor](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L115), [validated by: accepts valid limit and before](../../src/transport/ws/validation.test.ts#L30), [validated by: rejects a limit of 0](../../src/transport/ws/validation.test.ts#L37), [validated by: rejects a limit over 200](../../src/transport/ws/validation.test.ts#L42), [validated by: rejects a negative limit](../../src/transport/ws/validation.test.ts#L47)).
+
+
+A `list_sessions` frame is answered only when `transport.history.enabled` is `true`. When it is absent or `false`, the server MUST answer with an `error` frame carrying code `UNSUPPORTED` ([validated by: answers UNSUPPORTED when history is disabled](../../src/transport/conversationListHistory.test.ts#L28), [validated by: answers UNSUPPORTED when history is disabled](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.conversationList.test.ts#L37)). A server whose `SessionStore` does not implement `listFor` MUST also answer `UNSUPPORTED`, so a client can distinguish a store that cannot list from one that is empty ([validated by: answers UNSUPPORTED when sessionStore does not support listing](../../src/transport/conversationListHistory.test.ts#L42), [validated by: answers UNSUPPORTED when sessionStore is missing](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.conversationList.test.ts#L45), [validated by: answers UNSUPPORTED when listFor is missing on sessionStore](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.conversationList.test.ts#L63), [validated by: answers UNSUPPORTED when listFor throws StoreCannotList](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.conversationList.test.ts#L73)).
 
